{{also|setback}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-set back.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|sets back|setting back|set back|set back}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[delay]] or [[obstruct]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1898|author={{w|Winston Churchill (novelist)|Winston Churchill}}
|title={{w|The Celebrity}}|chapter=4
|passage=“Well,” I answered, at first with uncertainty, then with inspiration, “he would do splendidly to lead your cotillon, if you think of having one.” &para; “So you do not dance, Mr. Crocker?” &para; I was somewhat '''set back''' by her perspicuity.}}
#: {{ux|en|I expect it will '''set''' us '''back''' by a day or so, but I think a side trip will be worthwhile.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[remove]] from or allow [[distance]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Set''' it '''back''' from the road by twenty or thirty feet.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[install]] or position behind a boundary or surface, or in a [[recess]].
#: {{ux|en|The statue was '''set back''' in a niche.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|idiomatic}} To [[cost]] [[money]], as.
#: {{ux|en|How much do you suppose that fancy dress '''set''' her '''back'''?}}

